<title>FINLAND: PAY HIKES MUST SUPPORT LOW INFLATION - LIPPONEN.</title>
<headline>PAY HIKES MUST SUPPORT LOW INFLATION - LIPPONEN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pay hikes must be adjusted to low inflation, and the incomes settlement system must aim to boost employment, Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen said in a prepared speech to the Wood and Allied Workers' Union on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Wage policy must be adapted to the era of low inflation and the strong fundamental goal of settlement activities must be to prioritise improved employment,&quot; Lipponen said.</p>
<p>The current pay deal with moderate pay hikes across the board has boosted purchasing power by about three percent more than expected, since the deal has made possbile low inflation, lower interest rates and eased taxation, Lipponen said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
